{
  "version": 1,
  "meta": {
    "title": "Retry idempotent requests with exponential backoff",
    "summary": "- `request()`: retries failed **idempotent (GET) requests**, up to 3 times, exponential backoff\n- Retry logic in a new `retry.ts` module\n- New `HttpError` → only transient failures (5xx, 429) retried",
    "intent": "feature",
    "language": "en",
    "strategy": {
      "order": "top-down",
      "rationale": "What callers see (what changed) → the new module (how it works) → reach outside the diff (existing callers) and tests"
    },
    "takeaways": [
      "GET retries by default; other methods only with `idempotent: true`",
      "Only `isTransient()` errors are retried: 5xx and 429",
      "`fetchUser` gets retries without any code change; `renameUser` (PATCH) is unaffected"
    ],
    "reviewFocus": [
      "PATCH/POST callers that are idempotent: should pass `idempotent: true`?",
      "Total backoff (200+400+800 ms) within `timeoutMs`?"
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "effect": "check",
        "text": "`fetchUser` (unchanged caller, GET): now retried with no code change",
        "files": [
          "src/users/service.ts"
        ]
      },
      {
        "effect": "safe",
        "text": "`renameUser` (unchanged caller, PATCH): sent once, as before",
        "files": [
          "src/users/service.ts"
        ]
      },
      {
        "effect": "safe",
        "text": "Errors thrown: now `HttpError`, a subclass of `Error` → existing `catch` blocks still match"
      }
    ]
  },
  "source": {
    "base": "HEAD~1",
    "head": "HEAD"
  },
  "tour": {
    "order": [
      "src/api/client.ts",
      "src/api/retry.ts",
      "src/config.ts",
      "test/retry.test.ts"
    ]
  },
  "files": {
    "src/api/client.ts": {
      "status": "modified",
      "role": "HTTP entry point"
    },
    "src/api/retry.ts": {
      "status": "added",
      "role": "retry policy"
    },
    "src/config.ts": {
      "status": "modified",
